Implement user story EPAM-062: Slash Command: /config

## Story Description
Add `/config` to the REPL so users can inspect effective configuration and, where safe, change a small subset of session-scoped settings without leaving chat.

## Acceptance Criteria
- `/config` is registered in SlashCommands.ts
- `/config` shows the effective resolved session configuration summary
- `/config set` supports a safe subset of live session updates such as model or max-iterations if supported by the runtime
- Config precedence is respected and clearly explained in output
- Unit tests cover view mode and any supported set operations

## Technical Notes
- files: ["src/cli/repl/SlashCommands.ts","src/cli/repl/Repl.ts","src/config/ConfigResolver.ts"]
- requiredSkills: ["TypeScript","config-management","repl-integration"]

